{"path":"language/attributes/deprecated","title":"C attribute: deprecated (since C23)","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">C attribute:</span> deprecated <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-c23\">(since C23)</span>","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/c/language/attributes/deprecated","section":"language","kind":"page","summary":"Indicates that the name or entity declared with this attribute is deprecated, that is, the use is allowed, but discouraged for some reason.","html":"<p>Indicates that the name or entity declared with this attribute is <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deprecation\" class=\"extiw\" data-external=\"1\">deprecated</a>, that is, the use is allowed, but discouraged for some reason.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Syntax\">Syntax</h3>\n<table class=\"t-sdsc-begin\">\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"10\" class=\"t-sdsc-sep\">\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-sdsc\">\n<td> <code><b>[[</b></code> <code><b>deprecated</b></code> <code><b>]]</b></code><br><code><b>[[</b></code> <code><b>__deprecated__</b></code> <code><b>]]</b></code>\n</td>\n<td> (1)\n</td>\n<td class=\"t-sdsc-nopad\">\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"10\" class=\"t-sdsc-sep\">\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-sdsc\">\n<td> <code><b>[[</b></code> <code><b>deprecated</b></code> <code><b>(</b></code> <span class=\"t-spar\">string-literal</span> <code><b>)</b></code> <code><b>]]</b></code><br><code><b>[[</b></code> <code><b>__deprecated__</b></code> <code><b>(</b></code> <span class=\"t-spar\">string-literal</span> <code><b>)</b></code> <code><b>]]</b></code>\n</td>\n<td> (2)\n</td>\n<td class=\"t-sdsc-nopad\">\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"10\" class=\"t-sdsc-sep\">\n</td></tr></table>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> <span class=\"t-spar\">string-literal</span>\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> text that could be used to explain the rationale for deprecation and/or to suggest a replacing entity\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Explanation\">Explanation</h3>\n<p>Indicates that the use of the name or entity declared with this attribute is allowed, but discouraged for some reason. Compilers typically issue warnings on such uses. The <span class=\"t-spar\">string-literal</span>, if specified, is usually included in the warnings.\n</p><p>This attribute is allowed in declarations of the following names or entities:\n</p>\n<ul><li> <a href=\"/w/c/language/struct\">struct</a>/<a href=\"/w/c/language/union\">union</a>: <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"kw1\">struct</span> <span class=\"br0\">[</span><span class=\"br0\">[</span>deprecated<span class=\"br0\">]</span><span class=\"br0\">]</span> S<span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></code>,\n</li><li> <a href=\"/w/c/language/typedef\">typedef-name</a>: <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"br0\">[</span><span class=\"br0\">[</span>deprecated<span class=\"br0\">]</span><span class=\"br0\">]</span> <span class=\"kw1\">typedef</span> S<span class=\"sy2\">*</span> PS<span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></code>,\n</li><li> objects: <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"br0\">[</span><span class=\"br0\">[</span>deprecated<span class=\"br0\">]</span><span class=\"br0\">]</span> <span class=\"kw4\">int</span> x<span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></code>,\n</li><li> struct/union member: <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"kw1\">union</span> U <span class=\"br0\">{</span> <span class=\"br0\">[</span><span class=\"br0\">[</span>deprecated<span class=\"br0\">]</span><span class=\"br0\">]</span> <span class=\"kw4\">int</span> n<span class=\"sy4\">;</span> <span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></code>,\n</li><li> <a href=\"/w/c/language/function_definition\">function</a>: <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"br0\">[</span><span class=\"br0\">[</span>deprecated<span class=\"br0\">]</span><span class=\"br0\">]</span> <span class=\"kw4\">void</span> f<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw4\">void</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></code>,\n</li><li> <a href=\"/w/c/language/enum\">enumeration</a>: <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"kw2\">enum</span> <span class=\"br0\">[</span><span class=\"br0\">[</span>deprecated<span class=\"br0\">]</span><span class=\"br0\">]</span> E <span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></code>,\n</li><li> enumerator: <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"kw2\">enum</span> <span class=\"br0\">{</span> A <span class=\"br0\">[</span><span class=\"br0\">[</span>deprecated<span class=\"br0\">]</span><span class=\"br0\">]</span>, B <span class=\"br0\">[</span><span class=\"br0\">[</span>deprecated<span class=\"br0\">]</span><span class=\"br0\">]</span> <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"nu0\">42</span> <span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></code>.\n</li></ul>\n<p>A name declared non-deprecated may be redeclared deprecated. A name declared deprecated cannot be un-deprecated by redeclaring it without this attribute.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"c\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;stdio.h&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"br0\">[</span><span class=\"br0\">[</span>deprecated<span class=\"br0\">]</span><span class=\"br0\">]</span>\n<span class=\"kw4\">void</span> TriassicPeriod<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw4\">void</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/c/io/puts\"><span class=\"kw836\">puts</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"Triassic Period: [251.9 - 208.5] million years ago.\"</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"br0\">[</span><span class=\"br0\">[</span>deprecated<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"Use NeogenePeriod() instead.\"</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">]</span><span class=\"br0\">]</span>\n<span class=\"kw4\">void</span> JurassicPeriod<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw4\">void</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/c/io/puts\"><span class=\"kw836\">puts</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"Jurassic Period: [201.3 - 152.1] million years ago.\"</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"br0\">[</span><span class=\"br0\">[</span>deprecated<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"Use calcSomethingDifferently(int).\"</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">]</span><span class=\"br0\">]</span>\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> calcSomething<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw4\">int</span> x<span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"kw1\">return</span> x <span class=\"sy2\">*</span> <span class=\"nu0\">2</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw4\">void</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    TriassicPeriod<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    JurassicPeriod<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Possible output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>Triassic Period: [251.9 - 208.5] million years ago.\nJurassic Period: [201.3 - 152.1] million years ago.\n&nbsp;\nprog.c:23:5: warning: 'TriassicPeriod' is deprecated [-Wdeprecated-declarations]\n    TriassicPeriod();\n    ^\nprog.c:3:3: note: 'TriassicPeriod' has been explicitly marked deprecated here\n[[deprecated]]\n  ^\nprog.c:24:5: warning: 'JurassicPeriod' is deprecated: Use NeogenePeriod() instead. [-Wdeprecated-declarations]\n    JurassicPeriod();\n    ^\nprog.c:9:3: note: 'JurassicPeriod' has been explicitly marked deprecated here\n[[deprecated(\"Use NeogenePeriod() instead.\")]]\n  ^\n2 warnings generated.</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td colspan=\"2\"> <div class=\"t-dsc-see\"><span><a href=\"/w/cpp/language/attributes/deprecated\">C++ documentation</a></span> for <span class=\"t-dsc-see-tt\"><span>deprecated</span></span></div>\n</td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Syntax","id":"Syntax"},{"depth":3,"text":"Explanation","id":"Explanation"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C reference"},{"path":"language","title":"C language"},{"path":"language/attributes","title":"Attribute specifier sequence(since C23)"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"C attribute: deprecated (since C23)","children":[{"label":"Syntax","note":"string-literal"},{"label":"Explanation","note":"Indicates that the use of the name or entity declared with this attribute is allowed, but discouraged for some reason."},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also"}]},"standards":[],"wordCount":291,"codeBlockCount":2}
